<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Connection between the complementary-label estimator and complementary loss</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[K]=\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[K]=\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a model <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, denote its prediction by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any class <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(k,\hat{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(k,\hat{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.
In complementary-label learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ishida et al. (2019)</a></cite>, one observes
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}\neq y</annotation></semantics></math> sampled uniformly from <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[K]\setminus\{y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[K]\setminus\{y\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The complementary loss is defined (Eq. (10) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ishida et al. (2019)</a></cite>) as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\ell}(k,\hat{y})\;=\;-(K-1)\,\ell(k,\hat{y})\;+\;\sum_{j=1}^{K}\ell(j,\hat{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\ell}(k,\hat{y})\;=\;-(K-1)\,\ell(k,\hat{y})\;+\;\sum_{j=1}^{K}\ell(j,\hat{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Specialization to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> loss.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> loss <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell(k,\hat{y})=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(k,\hat{y})=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq k\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\ell}(k,\hat{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\ell}(k,\hat{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-(K-1)\,\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq k\}+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(K-1)\,\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq k\}+\sum_{j=1}^{K}\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq j\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-(K-1)\,\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq k\}+(K-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(K-1)\,\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq k\}+(K-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(K-1)\,\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}=k\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(K-1)\,\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}=k\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Risk under complementary labels.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The standard risk is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)}[\ell(y,\hat{y})]=\Pr(\hat{y}\neq y)=1-A," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)}[\ell(y,\hat{y})]=\Pr(\hat{y}\neq y)=1-A,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\Pr(\hat{y}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\Pr(\hat{y}=y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the accuracy.
By the risk-rewrite identity of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ishida et al. (2019)</a></cite> (Eq. (8)), we also have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\mathbb{E}_{(x,\bar{y})}[\bar{\ell}(\bar{y},\hat{y})]=(K-1)\,\Pr(\hat{y}=\bar{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\mathbb{E}_{(x,\bar{y})}[\bar{\ell}(\bar{y},\hat{y})]=(K-1)\,\Pr(\hat{y}=\bar{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Equivalence to our estimator.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq\bar{y}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq\bar{y}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\hat{y}=\bar{y})=1-\mathbb{E}[W]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\hat{y}=\bar{y})=1-\mathbb{E}[W]</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-A=(K-1)\,(1-\mathbb{E}[W])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-A=(K-1)\,(1-\mathbb{E}[W]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Rearranging yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(K-1)\,\mathbb{E}[W]-(K-2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(K-1)\,\mathbb{E}[W]-(K-2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This is exactly the linear correction in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In Corollary 1. ‣ 2.1 Estimator from Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
Replacing <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[W]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[W]</annotation></semantics></math> by its empirical mean
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}=\tfrac{1}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{c}}}W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}=\tfrac{1}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{c}}}W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
gives the unbiased estimator
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}=(K-1)\hat{q}-(K-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}=(K-1)\hat{q}-(K-2)</annotation></semantics></math>
of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Corollary 1. ‣ 2.1 Estimator from Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Data Labeling and Estimation Protocol</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In multiple-choice evaluation, the effective “class” is the <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">index position</em> of an option rather than its textual content. To satisfy the uniformity condition in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Setup and Notations ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), the labeling process proceeds as follows. For each item, all options are first shuffled uniformly at random. After shuffling, the correct index <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is recorded. A complementary label is then created by sampling a wrong index <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly from the <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math> remaining positions. The final published datum is <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,\text{shuffled options},\bar{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>shuffled options</mtext><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,\text{shuffled options},\bar{y})</annotation></semantics></math>. When the ground truth is known, this procedure can be automated: <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is only used internally for generating <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the released dataset never exposes <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. When labels are collected from human raters, the annotation interface can enforce the same randomization in the backend to guarantee uniformity. Any deviation, such as asking raters to pick the ‘most plausible wrong option,’ would violate the assumption behind Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Setup and Notations ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Exploring how to deal with alternative data or label collection mechanisms is left for future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The same protocol can be extended to cases where the ground truth is not available in advance. A complementary label is first generated in the same way, and then the annotator is asked to verify whether it happens to be correct. This verification yields a mixture of ordinary and complementary labels, which forms the mixed dataset studied in § <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Combining Ordinary and Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The end-to-end evaluation pipeline, including both ordinary and complementary sets and the associated estimators, is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix B Data Labeling and Estimation Protocol ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Two estimation strategies are supported: a closed-form maximum-likelihood estimator and an inverse-variance weighted (IVW) estimator.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Collecting complementary labels and estimating accuracy (fixed <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> MCQ items; evaluation model <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>; sizes <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}},n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}},n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each item <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Shuffle options uniformly; record correct index <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> item <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in</annotation></semantics></math> ordinary set <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Evaluate <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain prediction <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>; record <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}=y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}=y\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else<span id="alg1.l6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> complementary set
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             Sample <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly from <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,K\}\setminus\{y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,K\}\setminus\{y\}</annotation></semantics></math>; publish <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,\text{options},\bar{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>options</mtext><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,\text{options},\bar{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Evaluate <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain prediction <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>; record <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq\bar{y}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}\neq\bar{y}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
          Compute <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{o}}=\sum Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{o}}=\sum Z</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{c}}=\sum W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{c}}=\sum W</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Option A (ML):</span> return <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ML}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ML</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ML}}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eq. (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In Closed-Form Maximum-Likelihood Estimator (ML) ‣ 2.2 Combining Ordinary and Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) and a confidence interval from observed information.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Option B (IVW):</span> compute <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg1.l13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, then return <math id="alg1.l13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{IVW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{IVW}}</annotation></semantics></math> with plug-in confidence interval.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Two assumptions are critical for the validity of these estimators. First, the wrong index in each complementary label must be sampled uniformly; systematic biases, such as consistently preferring hard negatives, lead to biased estimates of <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Second, the ordinary and complementary sets must be drawn from the same distribution of items. If domain shift or subject imbalance exists, the combined estimator reflects accuracy on a mixture distribution. In such cases, stratified or subject-wise weighting may be preferable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>One-step Newton Update and IVW Equivalence</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the (unknown) accuracy for a <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-way multiple-choice task (<math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>).
We observe two independent samples:
(i) ordinary labels <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{o}}\sim\mathrm{Bin}(n_{\mathrm{o}},A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{o}}\sim\mathrm{Bin}(n_{\mathrm{o}},A)</annotation></semantics></math> with empirical accuracy <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}=S_{\mathrm{o}}/n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}=S_{\mathrm{o}}/n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) complementary labels obtained by uniformly sampling a wrong option per item, so that
<math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{c}}\sim\mathrm{Bin}(n_{\mathrm{c}},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{c}}\sim\mathrm{Bin}(n_{\mathrm{c}},q)</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(A)=\frac{A+K-2}{K-1},\qquad\widehat{q}=S_{\mathrm{c}}/n_{\mathrm{c}},\qquad\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}=(K-1)\widehat{q}-(K-2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(A)=\frac{A+K-2}{K-1},\qquad\widehat{q}=S_{\mathrm{c}}/n_{\mathrm{c}},\qquad\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}=(K-1)\widehat{q}-(K-2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We consider a pilot <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and write <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}=q(A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}=q(A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The joint log-likelihood is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(A)=S_{\mathrm{o}}\log A+(n_{\mathrm{o}}-S_{\mathrm{o}})\log(1-A)+S_{\mathrm{c}}\log q+(n_{\mathrm{c}}-S_{\mathrm{c}})\log(1-q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(A)=S_{\mathrm{o}}\log A+(n_{\mathrm{o}}-S_{\mathrm{o}})\log(1-A)+S_{\mathrm{c}}\log q+(n_{\mathrm{c}}-S_{\mathrm{c}})\log(1-q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Differentiating gives the score functions</p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathrm{o}}(A)=\frac{n_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}-A)}{A(1-A)},\qquad U_{\mathrm{c}}(A)=\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}-A)}{(K-1)^{2}\,q(1-q)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathrm{o}}(A)=\frac{n_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}-A)}{A(1-A)},\qquad U_{\mathrm{c}}(A)=\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}-A)}{(K-1)^{2}\,q(1-q)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The observed information terms are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{o}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A)=\frac{S_{\mathrm{o}}}{A^{2}}+\frac{n_{\mathrm{o}}-S_{\mathrm{o}}}{(1-A)^{2}},\qquad\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{c}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A)=\frac{1}{(K-1)^{2}}\!\left(\frac{S_{\mathrm{c}}}{q^{2}}+\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}-S_{\mathrm{c}}}{(1-q)^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{o}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A)=\frac{S_{\mathrm{o}}}{A^{2}}+\frac{n_{\mathrm{o}}-S_{\mathrm{o}}}{(1-A)^{2}},\qquad\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{c}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A)=\frac{1}{(K-1)^{2}}\!\left(\frac{S_{\mathrm{c}}}{q^{2}}+\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}-S_{\mathrm{c}}}{(1-q)^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">A one-step Newton update around <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}=A_{0}-\frac{U(A_{0})}{U^{\prime}(A_{0})}=A_{0}+\frac{U_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})+U_{\mathrm{c}}(A_{0})}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{o}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})+\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{c}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}=A_{0}-\frac{U(A_{0})}{U^{\prime}(A_{0})}=A_{0}+\frac{U_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})+U_{\mathrm{c}}(A_{0})}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{o}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})+\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{c}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When we set <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}=\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}=\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the ordinary part simplifies exactly:
since <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{o}}=n_{\mathrm{o}}A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{o}}=n_{\mathrm{o}}A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{o}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})=n_{\mathrm{o}}/[A_{0}(1-A_{0})]=I_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{o}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})=n_{\mathrm{o}}/[A_{0}(1-A_{0})]=I_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the Fisher information.
For the complementary part, we plug in <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\widehat{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\widehat{q}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{c}}=n_{\mathrm{c}}\widehat{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{c}}=n_{\mathrm{c}}\widehat{q}</annotation></semantics></math> holds identically.
This yields</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{c}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})\big|_{q=\widehat{q}}=\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}}{(K-1)^{2}\,\widehat{q}(1-\widehat{q})}=I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q}),\qquad U_{\mathrm{c}}(A_{0})\big|_{q=\widehat{q}}=I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})\,(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}-A_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>obs</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{c}}^{\mathrm{obs}}(A_{0})\big|_{q=\widehat{q}}=\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}}{(K-1)^{2}\,\widehat{q}(1-\widehat{q})}=I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q}),\qquad U_{\mathrm{c}}(A_{0})\big|_{q=\widehat{q}}=I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})\,(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}-A_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting back into the Newton update gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}\approx A_{0}+\frac{I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}-A_{0})}{I_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})+I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}\approx A_{0}+\frac{I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}-A_{0})}{I_{\mathrm{o}}(A_{0})+I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Rearranging shows that the practical one-step update is a convex combination of the two empirical estimators:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{IVW}}\;\approx\;\frac{I_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}+I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}}{I_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})+I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{IVW}}\;\approx\;\frac{I_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}+I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}}{I_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})+I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the two constituent estimators, the variance–information identities are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})=\frac{1}{I_{\mathrm{o}}},\qquad\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}})=\frac{1}{I_{\mathrm{c}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})=\frac{1}{I_{\mathrm{o}}},\qquad\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}})=\frac{1}{I_{\mathrm{c}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with the plug-in Fisher information</p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})=\frac{n_{\mathrm{o}}}{\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}(1-\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})},\qquad I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})=\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}}{(K-1)^{2}\,\widehat{q}(1-\widehat{q})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{o}}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})=\frac{n_{\mathrm{o}}}{\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}(1-\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})},\qquad I_{\mathrm{c}}(\widehat{q})=\frac{n_{\mathrm{c}}}{(K-1)^{2}\,\widehat{q}(1-\widehat{q})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore the IVW weight can be written either in information form,
<math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}=\frac{I_{\mathrm{o}}}{I_{\mathrm{o}}+I_{\mathrm{c}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}=\frac{I_{\mathrm{o}}}{I_{\mathrm{o}}+I_{\mathrm{c}}},</annotation></semantics></math>
or, equivalently, in variance form (using <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\bullet}=1/\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\bullet})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\bullet}=1/\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\bullet})</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}=\frac{I_{\mathrm{o}}}{I_{\mathrm{o}}+I_{\mathrm{c}}}=\frac{\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}})}{\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})+\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}=\frac{I_{\mathrm{o}}}{I_{\mathrm{o}}+I_{\mathrm{c}}}=\frac{\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}})}{\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})+\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging these into the convex combination yields exactly results in §<a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Combining Ordinary and Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{IVW}}=\;w^{\star}\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}+(1-w^{\star})\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>comp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{IVW}}=\;w^{\star}\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}+(1-w^{\star})\,\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{comp}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the IVW estimator is a one-step Newton approximation to the joint ML:
it is first-order equivalent and asymptotically efficient, but may differ in finite samples
because the weights are fixed by plug-in information rather than optimized jointly.
While the ML is theoretically optimal, the IVW rule is a simple linear combination that
often delivers practically comparable performance and is easier to apply in practice.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 2.3.2 Mixture estimator bounds via union bound ‣ 2.3 Theoretical analysis ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{j}=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}_{j}=y_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}_{j}=y_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dots,n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dots,n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>, are i.i.d. Bernoulli(<math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>) with <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Z_{j}]=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Z_{j}]=A</annotation></semantics></math>; and
<math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{i}=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}_{i}\neq\bar{y}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=\mathbb{I}\{\hat{y}_{i}\neq\bar{y}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, are i.i.d. Bernoulli(<math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>) with <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=(A+K-2)/(K-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=(A+K-2)/(K-1)</annotation></semantics></math> under Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Setup and Notations ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). The two groups are independent.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the rescaled variables</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(o)}_{j}:=\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}}Z_{j},\qquad X^{(c)}_{i}:=\tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}W_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(o)}_{j}:=\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}}Z_{j},\qquad X^{(c)}_{i}:=\tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}W_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and collect them as <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n_{\mathrm{o}}+n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n_{\mathrm{o}}+n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the centered sum</span></p>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\sum_{j=1}^{n_{\mathrm{o}}}\!\bigl(X^{(o)}_{j}-\mathbb{E}X^{(o)}_{j}\bigr)\;+\;\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\!\bigl(X^{(c)}_{i}-\mathbb{E}X^{(c)}_{i}\bigr)\;=\;\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\sum_{j=1}^{n_{\mathrm{o}}}\!\bigl(X^{(o)}_{j}-\mathbb{E}X^{(o)}_{j}\bigr)\;+\;\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\!\bigl(X^{(c)}_{i}-\mathbb{E}X^{(c)}_{i}\bigr)\;=\;\widehat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We verify the conditions of Theorem 2.10 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boucheron et al. (2003)</a></cite>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i) Independence)</em><span id="A4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> holds by construction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii) Boundedness).</em><span id="A4.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> For all <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|X^{(o)}_{j}-\mathbb{E}X^{(o)}_{j}\bigr|\leq\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\qquad\bigl|X^{(c)}_{i}-\mathbb{E}X^{(c)}_{i}\bigr|\leq\tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|X^{(o)}_{j}-\mathbb{E}X^{(o)}_{j}\bigr|\leq\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\qquad\bigl|X^{(c)}_{i}-\mathbb{E}X^{(c)}_{i}\bigr|\leq\tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set</span></p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=\max~\!\Bigl\{\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\ \tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\Bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.160em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=\max~\!\Bigl\{\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\ \tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iii) Second moment).</em><span id="A4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Summing variances,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v:=\sum_{j=1}^{n_{\mathrm{o}}}\!\mathrm{Var}(X^{(o)}_{j})+\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\!\mathrm{Var}(X^{(c)}_{i})=w^{2}\tfrac{A(1-A)}{n_{\mathrm{o}}}+(1-w)^{2}\tfrac{(K-1)^{2}\,q(1-q)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v:=\sum_{j=1}^{n_{\mathrm{o}}}\!\mathrm{Var}(X^{(o)}_{j})+\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\!\mathrm{Var}(X^{(c)}_{i})=w^{2}\tfrac{A(1-A)}{n_{\mathrm{o}}}+(1-w)^{2}\tfrac{(K-1)^{2}\,q(1-q)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iv) Higher moments).</em><span id="A4.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Since <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert X_{i}-\mathbb{E}X_{i}\rvert\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert X_{i}-\mathbb{E}X_{i}\rvert\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>, for all integers <math id="A4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{i}-\mathbb{E}X_{i})_{+}^{q}\leq c^{\,q-2}(X_{i}-\mathbb{E}X_{i})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{i}-\mathbb{E}X_{i})_{+}^{q}\leq c^{\,q-2}(X_{i}-\mathbb{E}X_{i})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; summing and taking expectations yields
<math id="A4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\mathbb{E}[(X_{i})_{+}^{q}]\leq v\,c^{\,q-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\mathbb{E}[(X_{i})_{+}^{q}]\leq v\,c^{\,q-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is dominated by the requirement
<math id="A4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{q!}{2}\,v\,c^{\,q-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{q!}{2}\,v\,c^{\,q-2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boucheron et al., 2003</a>, Thm. 2.10)</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, Theorem 2.10 applies to <math id="A4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A4.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) and (using the symmetric lower tail plus a union bound) gives
<math id="A4.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\{\,|S|\geq\sqrt{2vt}+ct\,\}\leq 2e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\{\,|S|\geq\sqrt{2vt}+ct\,\}\leq 2e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting <math id="A4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\log(2/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\log(2/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> yields Eq. (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 2.3.2 Mixture estimator bounds via union bound ‣ 2.3 Theoretical analysis ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Practical plug-in forms of the Bernstein bound</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The quantities <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> are unknown; replace them by their empirical counterparts. Define
<math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}=\tfrac{\hat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}(1-\hat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\qquad\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}=\tfrac{(K-1)^{2}\,\hat{q}(1-\hat{q})}{n_{\mathrm{c}}},\qquad\hat{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}=w^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+(1-w)^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ord</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}=\tfrac{\hat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}}(1-\hat{A}_{\mathrm{ord}})}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\qquad\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}=\tfrac{(K-1)^{2}\,\hat{q}(1-\hat{q})}{n_{\mathrm{c}}},\qquad\hat{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}=w^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+(1-w)^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}},</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}=S_{\mathrm{c}}/n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}=S_{\mathrm{c}}/n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting into Eq.  (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 2.3.2 Mixture estimator bounds via union bound ‣ 2.3 Theoretical analysis ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) yields the computable bound
<math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\hat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A\bigr|\;\leq\;\sqrt{\,2\,\hat{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}\,\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\,}\;+\;c\,\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\hat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A\bigr|\;\leq\;\sqrt{\,2\,\hat{v}_{\mathrm{mix}}\,\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\,}\;+\;c\,\log\tfrac{2}{\delta},</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is as in Eq. (<a href="#A4.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>). For clarity, an equivalent compact statement is</p>
<table id="A5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;|\hat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A|\;\leq\;\sqrt{\,2\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\bigl[w^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+(1-w)^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}\bigr]\,}\;+\;\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\max~\!\Bigl(\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\ \tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.160em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;|\hat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A|\;\leq\;\sqrt{\,2\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\bigl[w^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+(1-w)^{2}\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}\bigr]\,}\;+\;\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\max~\!\Bigl(\tfrac{w}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\ \tfrac{(1-w)(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The variance component is minimized at
<math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}=\frac{v_{\mathrm{c}}}{v_{\mathrm{o}}+v_{\mathrm{c}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}=\frac{v_{\mathrm{c}}}{v_{\mathrm{o}}+v_{\mathrm{c}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a practical <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as
<math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}}=\frac{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}}=\frac{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}},</annotation></semantics></math>
coinciding with the IVW weight in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In Inverse Variance Weighted Estimator (IVW) ‣ 2.2 Combining Ordinary and Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). At this choice, the dominant (variance) term equals
<math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\,2\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\cdot\frac{v_{\mathrm{o}}v_{\mathrm{c}}}{v_{\mathrm{o}}+v_{\mathrm{c}}}\,}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\,2\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\cdot\frac{v_{\mathrm{o}}v_{\mathrm{c}}}{v_{\mathrm{o}}+v_{\mathrm{c}}}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Defining <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{h}_{\mathrm{min}}:=\tfrac{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}\,\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{h}_{\mathrm{min}}:=\tfrac{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}\,\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
using the fully plug-in version gives</p>
<table id="A5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A|\;\leq\;\sqrt{\,2\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\widehat{h}_{\mathrm{min}}\,}\;+\;\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\max~\!\Bigl(\tfrac{\hat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}}}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\ \tfrac{(1-\hat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}})(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.160em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{A}_{\mathrm{mix}}-A|\;\leq\;\sqrt{\,2\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\widehat{h}_{\mathrm{min}}\,}\;+\;\log\tfrac{2}{\delta}\;\max~\!\Bigl(\tfrac{\hat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}}}{n_{\mathrm{o}}},\ \tfrac{(1-\hat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}})(K-1)}{n_{\mathrm{c}}}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Conceptually, the mgf-based Bernstein bound (Eq. (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 2.3.2 Mixture estimator bounds via union bound ‣ 2.3 Theoretical analysis ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>))
tightens Hoeffding’s inequality by adding both a variance term <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and a range-driven linear term <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> grows, the right-hand side vanishes: the variance part decays as <math id="A5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/n_{\mathrm{o}})+O(1/n_{\mathrm{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/n_{\mathrm{o}})+O(1/n_{\mathrm{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
while the linear term scales as <math id="A5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\big(\max~\{w/n_{\mathrm{o}},\,(1-w)(K-1)/n_{\mathrm{c}}\}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.330em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\big(\max~\{w/n_{\mathrm{o}},\,(1-w)(K-1)/n_{\mathrm{c}}\}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The plug-in IVW weight <math id="A5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}}=\tfrac{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>IVW</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{w}_{\mathrm{IVW}}=\tfrac{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}{\hat{v}_{\mathrm{o}}+\hat{v}_{\mathrm{c}}}</annotation></semantics></math>
converges to <math id="A5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}=\tfrac{v_{\mathrm{c}}}{v_{\mathrm{o}}+v_{\mathrm{c}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}=\tfrac{v_{\mathrm{c}}}{v_{\mathrm{o}}+v_{\mathrm{c}}}</annotation></semantics></math>; in particular, <math id="A5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}\!\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}\!\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}\!\to\!\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}\!\to\!\infty</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed (the complementary arm dominates), and <math id="A5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}\!\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}\!\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}\!\to\!\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}\!\to\!\infty</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A5.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed (the ordinary arm dominates).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Estimator Configurations</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we summarize the exact configurations of all estimators used in
Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2 Statistical Validation of Complementary and Mixed Estimators ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Ord</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ordinary-label estimator based on <math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}=300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}=300</annotation></semantics></math> samples per dataset
(<math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}=120" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}=120</annotation></semantics></math> for GPQA due to dataset size). Accuracy is computed directly from the proportion of correct ordinary labels.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Comp-<math id="A6.I1.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complementary-label estimator with the same number of samples as the ordinary case, i.e. <math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}=n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}=n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}=120" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}=120</annotation></semantics></math> for GPQA). This setting highlights the loss of efficiency when only complementary labels are available.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Comp-(K-1)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complementary-label estimator with sample size fixed at <math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K-1)</annotation></semantics></math> times the ordinary case, i.e. <math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}=(K-1)n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}=(K-1)n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Following the protocol in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Data Labeling and Estimation Protocol ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, each instance with oracle label <math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is converted into <math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K-1)</annotation></semantics></math> complementary “No” labels <math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\bar{y}\in\mathcal{Y}\setminus\{y\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{y}\in\mathcal{Y}\setminus\{y\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the ordinary label is discarded; thus no ordinary labels are present in this setting.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Comp-Var</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complementary-label estimator with sample size <math id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> chosen such that its variance matches that of <math id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{o}}</annotation></semantics></math> ordinary labels, following Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Estimator from Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). This represents the idealized regime where complementary labels are sufficiently abundant to offset their lower per-sample information.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">IVW-0.5</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A baseline inverse-variance weighted estimator with a fixed equal weight <math id="A6.I1.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> between ordinary and complementary accuracies. This serves as a naïve combination strategy without using variance information.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">IVW</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Inverse-variance weighted estimator with closed-form plug-in weights (Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In Inverse Variance Weighted Estimator (IVW) ‣ 2.2 Combining Ordinary and Complementary Labels ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)), combining ordinary and complementary estimates optimally under the variance–information identities.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ML</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximum-likelihood estimator obtained by solving the joint likelihood equation using both ordinary and complementary samples. Asymptotically equivalent to IVW but involving a nonlinear update (Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C One-step Newton Update and IVW Equivalence ‣ Scalable Oversightvia Partitioned Human Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Ord-Eval</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.ix8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Oracle reference: accuracy evaluated directly on the entire dataset using ordinary labels. This is shown only for comparison and is excluded from macro-averages.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notes on datasets.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Math</span> denotes <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Math-MC</span> evaluated with <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4.1-nano</span> instead of <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-5-nano</span>, due to reasoning-output constraints.
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>‡</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddagger</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Math (CoT)</span> denotes the same <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Math-MC</span> dataset evaluated under chain-of-thought prompting (applied only to Math; model=<span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4.1-nano</span>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Implementation details on ADAS and AFlow</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure a fair comparison, we constructed validation and test splits for each benchmark,
following the numbers and ratios used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
Specifically, we sampled 120 validation and 800 test examples for Math-MC and Medical Abstract,
and 88 validation and 458 test examples for GPQA.
For AFlow, we set the number of validation runs to 3 and used the same validation set as ADAS, rather than the separate validation subset reported in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025c)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For code and prompts, we largely follow the official implementations of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2025)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025c)</a></cite>, with two minor modifications for reproducibility in our setting.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ADAS.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The set of experts was adapted to better align with our benchmarks (e.g., replacing domain-specific experts in LLM Debate with ones relevant to GPQA and Medical Abstract).
All other prompt components remain unchanged.
We uploaded the full text of the adapted prompts and scripts in the supplementary material.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">AFlow.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the original AFlow does not directly correspond to the multiple-choice format,
we modified the answer extraction and normalization functions, and used the following prompt:</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F5F5F5;--ltx-border-color:#C8C8C8;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Answer</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">following</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">multiple</span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">choice</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">question</span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">problem</span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[’</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Question</span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’]}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">A</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">problem</span><span id="lstnumberx3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[’</span><span id="lstnumberx3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">A</span><span id="lstnumberx3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’]}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">B</span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">problem</span><span id="lstnumberx4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[’</span><span id="lstnumberx4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">B</span><span id="lstnumberx4.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’]}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">C</span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">problem</span><span id="lstnumberx5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[’</span><span id="lstnumberx5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">C</span><span id="lstnumberx5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’]}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">D</span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">problem</span><span id="lstnumberx6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[’</span><span id="lstnumberx6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">D</span><span id="lstnumberx6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’]}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">At</span><span id="lstnumberx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">very</span><span id="lstnumberx8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">end</span><span id="lstnumberx8.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx8.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">output</span><span id="lstnumberx8.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">final</span><span id="lstnumberx8.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">answer</span><span id="lstnumberx8.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">in</span><span id="lstnumberx8.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx8.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">format</span><span id="lstnumberx8.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">###</span><span id="lstnumberx10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">X</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx11" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Where</span><span id="lstnumberx12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">X</span><span id="lstnumberx12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">is</span><span id="lstnumberx12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">exactly</span><span id="lstnumberx12.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">one</span><span id="lstnumberx12.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">of</span><span id="lstnumberx12.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">A</span><span id="lstnumberx12.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx12.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">B</span><span id="lstnumberx12.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx12.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">C</span><span id="lstnumberx12.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx12.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">or</span><span id="lstnumberx12.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">D</span><span id="lstnumberx12.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx13" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx14" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Do</span><span id="lstnumberx14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">not</span><span id="lstnumberx14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">add</span><span id="lstnumberx14.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">anything</span><span id="lstnumberx14.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">after</span><span id="lstnumberx14.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">this</span><span id="lstnumberx14.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">line</span><span id="lstnumberx14.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span><span id="lstnumberx14.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">The</span><span id="lstnumberx14.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">last</span><span id="lstnumberx14.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">line</span><span id="lstnumberx14.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">of</span><span id="lstnumberx14.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">your</span><span id="lstnumberx14.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">output</span><span id="lstnumberx14.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">must</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">only</span><span id="lstnumberx15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">contain</span><span id="lstnumberx15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’###</span><span id="lstnumberx15.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">X</span><span id="lstnumberx15.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’.</span><span id="lstnumberx15.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">If</span><span id="lstnumberx15.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">you</span><span id="lstnumberx15.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">write</span><span id="lstnumberx15.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">anything</span><span id="lstnumberx15.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">after</span><span id="lstnumberx15.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx15.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">line</span><span id="lstnumberx15.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’###</span><span id="lstnumberx15.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">X</span><span id="lstnumberx15.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’,</span><span id="lstnumberx15.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">your</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx16" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">answer</span><span id="lstnumberx16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">will</span><span id="lstnumberx16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">be</span><span id="lstnumberx16.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">marked</span><span id="lstnumberx16.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">as</span><span id="lstnumberx16.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">incorrect</span><span id="lstnumberx16.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span>
</div>
